{
  "source": "Digital Earth Africa, Water Observations from Space (WOfS) annual summary, derived from USGS/NASA Landsat, 30 m",
  "sensor": "optical (Landsat 5/7/8/9)",
  "pixel_m": 120.0,
  "method": "Per calendar year. Water = wet in >= 10% of cloud-free looks and at least 2 times. Permanent = wet in >= 80% of looks. Seasonal = water minus permanent. Areas counted in equal-area EPSG:6933.",
  "caveat": "Optical sensors map OPEN water. Water under reeds, papyrus and trees is largely missed, so these areas are not comparable in level with the NISAR flooded-vegetation class and must not be plotted as one series with NISAR.",
  "low_coverage_note": "Years flagged low_coverage have fewer than 8 cloud-free Landsat looks; their area is a lower bound. The flood lasts only a few months, so a year with few looks can miss it entirely.",
  "reliable_since": 2013,
  "reliable_note": "From 2013 (Landsat 8) every year has 23+ looks. Compare years confidently from 2013 on; treat earlier year-to-year jumps with caution.",
